-- HTB deliberate change: upstream condition alignment (item C19, found while building op 12).
--
-- Steven asked on 2026-10-19 to take upstream changes that have no effect, so HTB drifts less. These formats
-- still had the old upstream (v1) conditions; this takes Dictionarry's (fb09c84) and keeps HTB's own choices:
-- FraMeSToR in the 1080p and 720p Quality tiers (op 8), SiCFoI as a group in Remux Tier 4 (op 7), Not
-- Original, CAM, the ban formats and the HDR family. Measured on every library file and the 75 saved searches:
-- no decision changes. The score changes land on files that are already banned (961 TV WEBRips match Banned
-- WEBRip today), on DVD remuxes (they lose the +20,000 DVD credit, in line with "skip DVD remuxes"), and on
-- 576p WEB-DLs, which stop matching 480p WEB-DL as well (op 9 would otherwise count them twice).
-- Left out: 1080p Efficient TV WEB Tier 5 (upstream adds a season-pack rule that can't be measured offline).

